any's products include ML-007C-MA, a fixed-dose combination of an M 1 /M 4 muscarinic agonist for the treatment of schizophrenia and Alzheimer's disease psychosis; ML-004 for the treatment of social communication deficit and/or irritability in autism spectrum disorder; ML-021 for the treatment of motor deficits in Parkinson's disease; ML-055 for the treatment of neuropsychiatric conditions; and ML-009, a G-protein-coupled receptor 52 positive allosteric modulator for the treatment of hyperactivity, impulsivity and agitation-related disorders. The company also develops platform identifying neural circuits causally linked to disease and targeting those circuits for therapeutic modulation. The company was formerly known as Alvarado Therapeutics, Inc. and changed its name to MapLight Therapeutics, Inc. in August 2019. MapLight Therapeutics, Inc. was incorporated in 2018 and is based in Redwood City, California.","ceo_bio":"Dr. Christopher A. Kroeger M.B.A., M.D., Ph.D. | Founder, President, CEO & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 133 people. Stock-based compensation of $271K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["MapLight Therapeutics, Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $330M market cap.","Returns on capital run at -2534% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $139M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 52% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Healthcare peers \u201